  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "The current best is config_041 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, acc=0.7250). All major design axes have been explored and point to this configuration: multiprofile >> singleprofile, transformer > avgpool, scvi_n200 >> scgpt, ViT-L > resnet50, weighted ≥ concat. The one major untested dimension with all other settings at their known-best values is the RNA encoder: pca_n2000 has never been paired with (imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted, multiprofile). Testing config_039 (pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted) directly clarifies whether a linear PCA representation can match or exceed the learned scvi embedding in this strong multimodal pipeline. If it performs comparably, it confirms scvi_n200's advantage is modest and we can focus remaining budget on fine-tuning around config_041; if it is clearly worse, it locks in scvi_n200 and lets us exploit the remaining 3 experiments on micro-variants. Expected cost is moderate (~3.0–3.5 GPU hours), slightly below config_041's 3.60 h since PCA is a cheap linear projection compared to the scvi encoder, making this a high-information, relatively cheap experiment."
}

